<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tervel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 700–721</span> · Also known as Khan Tervel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tervel was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> from about 700 to about 721, the son and successor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asparuh-of-bulgaria">Asparuh</a>. In 705 he helped the deposed emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii">Justinian II</a> regain the Byzantine throne, receiving the title of caesar and a territory south of the Balkan mountains. In 717–718 he sent forces that helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> break the Arab siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>.</p></div>
